 r"I am writing to apply for the Healthcare Analyst role in GlobalData Healthcare's Oncology \& Hematology team in London. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. The role you describe, researching disease markets, speaking with physicians and experts, forecasting the opportunity for drugs in development and writing it up for pharmaceutical clients, brings together the parts of my background I enjoy most.",

 r"Oncology is the area of life sciences I have kept coming back to. In 2024 I worked as a research data analyst at the University of Science and Technology of China, building a spatial transcriptomics pipeline for medulloblastoma, and more recently I worked on an AI product for patients with bone metastases. I like that this role asks for both scientific understanding and a commercial view of where a disease market is going, and that the output is research that pharmaceutical teams actually use to make decisions.",

 r"The closest experience I have to the role itself is at Ipsos Strategy3, where I analysed healthcare datasets and more than 80 interviews with healthcare professionals. I built a structured coding framework to turn interview transcripts into quantitative variables, and built market-sizing and forecasting models for emerging health-product segments. I then turned the findings into dashboards, reports and recommendations with the research and strategy teams, so I am used to moving from interviews and desk research to a clear written conclusion.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked with a pharmaceutical client and their clinical experts on a patient-facing AI product in oncology. I helped define what a safe, accurate answer looked like, built a 246-question benchmark that became the client's acceptance standard, and wrote the evaluation reports I presented to the client. At TikTok Shop UK I now present analysis to operations, product and commercial teams, which has taught me to lead with the conclusion and keep the detail for anyone who wants it. My MSc dissertation used data from 458,840 UK Biobank participants, and I am confident with Excel and Python for analysis and forecasting.",

